# Note delay (7): the row's trigger moves to tick xx, with the instrument the row selects.
# 700 is an ordinary trigger; a delay at or past the row's length drops the note; 7 without
# a note does nothing; a delayed trigger and a cut on the same tick are written in channel
# order; a delayed wave trigger loads its wave then; a later retrigger uses the delayed
# note's period.
ticks_per_row 04

pulse 1 00 80 F3
pulse 2 80 40 A7            # length enabled
wave_instrument 1 00 20
noise 1 40 F1               # length enabled
wave 0 0123456789ABCDEFFEDCBA9876543210

order 01 02 03 04

pattern 01                  # channel 1
00 C-4 1 700                # ordinary trigger
04 E-4 2 702                # instrument 2, triggered at tick 2
08 G-4 . 704                # at the row's length: dropped
0C --- . 702                # no note: nothing
10 A-4 . 701                # tick 1, with channel 2's cut
14 --- . C70                # retrigger with A-4's period

pattern 02                  # channel 2
10 C-4 1 E01                # cut at tick 1, after channel 1's delayed trigger

pattern 03                  # channel 3
04 C-4 1 703                # wave loaded at tick 3

pattern 04                  # channel 4
08 D-4 1 701
18 E-4 . 703
